Okay this is horrible so I'm putting it in spoiler tags just in case people would rather not know... The good news is that Harley likely didn't dehydrate to death.

&gt;!The bad news is that he likely died of suffocation or from a brain hemorrhage. Our bodies are not made to hang upside down and it sort of sounds like he went in head first. Hanging upside down causes your organs to move up and put pressure on your lungs increasing the risk of suffocation. John Jones, the man who died after 28 hours being stuck hanging upside down in a cave, is believed to have died from suffocation from his own organs pressing on his lungs.!&lt;

&gt;!Even if you have enough oxygen, hanging upside down for too long can cause strain on the heart which can cause heart failure. Additionally, while our feet have evolved to have a system to force blood back up into the body, our heads do not. Hanging upside down for too long will cause blood vessels in our brains to hemorrhage and kill us. We're not talking about an hour will kill you, but other people who have died from being trapped hanging upside down usually die in a day instead of the 2-3 days it would take you to die of dehydration.!&lt;
